# Template for ga4_realtime.py's variables. Copy it to .env and fill it in; the
# real .env is gitignored, this file is not.

# The NUMERIC property ID — GA4 → Admin → Property settings.
# NOT the measurement ID (G-XXXXXXXXXX) that gtag.js uses on the site: that one
# is for the browser and not for the API, and using it here produces a
# PermissionDenied that never explains the cause. The script rejects the G-
# format by name, before any call, precisely because the API's own error does
# not help.
GA4_PROPERTY_ID=

# The service account's JSON key. A relative path resolves against the script's
# own directory, never against the directory it was called from.
#
# The same key serves two APIs, and both have to be enabled in the GCP project:
# the Data API (reports) and the Admin API (the property's name and timezone).
# Without the Admin API ga4_realtime.py still runs, but warns and falls back to
# UTC — which makes the day roll over at the wrong moment.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=secrets/ga4-service-account.json
